WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.650
One more system, for waters you may never see but the exam still asks about.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.800
The Western Rivers.

3
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.000
That’s the Mississippi and its tributaries.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.925
The marks there are a modified version of what you know.

5
00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:17.150
The buoys aren’t numbered.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.950
Why not?

7
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.250
Because the channel keeps moving.

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.225
A river shifts its sandbars from one month to the next, and the buoys are moved to follow.

9
00:00:28.475 --> 00:00:35.450
Instead of numbers, there are mileage boards on the bank, showing the distance in statute miles from a fixed point.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.200
Statute miles, not nautical.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:44.675
Passing daymarks, red triangles and green squares, mark the side of the channel along a bank.

12
00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:51.500
And crossing daymarks, shaped like diamonds, show where the channel crosses from one bank to the other.
